Promoted from P3 audit bundle #1193. Original findings:

`lib/core/network/adapters/dio_network_client.dart:44-60`, `lib/core/config/app_config.dart:126-148`: default `API_TIMEOUT` (30s) equals `API_RECEIVE_TIMEOUT` (30s), so the documented receive-timeout retry never runs with the shipped defaults; `API_TIMEOUT=0` fails every request before sending (`hits=0 err=NetworkException(RECEIVE_TIMEOUT)... within 0s`). Criterion: a non-positive value means no deadline or is rejected, defaults leave room for one retry (or the docs say retries need `API_TIMEOUT > API_RECEIVE_TIMEOUT`); tests pin both.

## Acceptance criteria

- a non-positive value means no deadline or is rejected, defaults leave room for one retry (or the docs say retries need `API_TIMEOUT > API_RECEIVE_TIMEOUT`); tests pin both.
- Required host checks and applicable workflow dispatches pass; evidence names each criterion. Parent #1193 is checked only after this issue closes.


